<article class="env-lemma" id="049U">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/049U">Lemma <span data-tag="049U">76.13.4</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme contained in $\mathit{Sch}_{fppf}$. Let $F, G, H : (\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}^{opp} \to \textit{Sets}$. Let $a : F \to G$, $b : H \to G$ be transformations of functors. Consider the fibre product diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ H \times _{b, G, a} F \ar[r]_-{b'} \ar[d]_{a'} &  F \ar[d]^ a \\  H \ar[r]^ b &  G }  \]
</div>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
If $a$ is formally smooth, then the base change $a'$ is formally smooth. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If $a$ is formally étale, then the base change $a'$ is formally étale. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If $a$ is formally unramified, then the base change $a'$ is formally unramified. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is formal. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>